# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. A connection string contains a password -- it must never be
# committed, and it should not be pasted into a chat, an issue, or a screenshot.

# Leave unset to use a local SQLite file (api/field_estimate.db). That is the
# default and needs nothing installed.
#
# To use Postgres, paste the connection string exactly as your provider prints
# it -- the app rewrites the scheme itself. From Neon it looks like:
#
# FIELD_ESTIMATE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@ep-xxxx.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
#
# Put the real value in .env, never in this file -- this one is committed.
